  "question": {
    "text": "Three charge q, Q and 4q are placed in a straight line of length $l$ at points distant $0, \\frac{1}{2}$ and $l$ respectively from one end. In order to make the net froce on q zero, the charge Q must be equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$-\\mathrm{q}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$-2 q$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{-\\mathrm{q}}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "q",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{F}_{\\text {net }}\\right)_{\\mathrm{q}}=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\mathrm{k} \\frac{\\mathrm{Qq}}{\\left(\\frac{\\ell}{2}\\right)^{2}}+\\mathrm{k} \\frac{4 \\mathrm{q}^{2}}{\\ell^{2}}=0$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0013_c13a28a21cc6.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\text { where } \\mathrm{k}=\\frac{1}{4 \\pi \\varepsilon_{0}} \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow 4 \\mathrm{Qq}+4 \\mathrm{q}^{2}=0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{Q}=-\\mathrm{q}\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$"
  }
}